# The walkthrough is a build output, not a document.
#
# This is the opposite call to docs/build/, where the PDFs ARE committed so reviewers can
# open them without a toolchain. The difference is diffability and lifespan. A take is about
# 18MB of WebM plus MP4 plus stills, none of it diffable, and git would keep a complete new
# copy on every re-record rather than a delta. It is also stale the moment anyone touches the
# UI, which on this repo is most weeks.
#
# What is committed instead is the recorder (tools/demo/) and the narration (SCRIPT.md), so
# anyone can regenerate the video in about two minutes:
#
#   CI=true pnpm --filter @maren/web build
#   node tools/demo/record.mjs
#
# If a specific take ever needs to be preserved — the one actually shown at a demo day, say —
# put it somewhere built for binaries and link it from SCRIPT.md. Do not commit it here.

*.webm
*.mp4
frames/
